For periodical reporting with a single reporting quantity set to true in reportQuantityRS‑Indexes, the sorting quantity is determined as follows:

- If the single quantity configured in **reportQuantityRS‑Indexes** is **rsrp**, RSRP is used as the sorting quantity.  
- If the single quantity is **rsrq**, RSRQ is used as the sorting quantity.  
- If the single quantity is **sinr**, SINR is used as the sorting quantity.

This is derived from the rule in clause 5.5.5.2 (context [1]), which states:  
> if reportType is set to periodical:  
> if a single reporting quantity is set to true in reportQuantityRS-Indexes;  
> consider the configured single quantity as the sorting quantity;  
> if rsrp is set to true;  
> consider RSRP as the sorting quantity;  
> consider RSRQ as the sorting quantity;

The nested structure indicates that when a single quantity is configured, that specific quantity (rsrp, rsrq, or sinr) becomes the sorting quantity. The subsequent lines “if rsrp is set to true; consider RSRP as the sorting quantity; consider RSRQ as the sorting quantity” apply only when a single quantity is **not** explicitly set to true (i.e., when multiple quantities may be reported).
